{"title":"1 - OVERVIEW","description":"","path":"sets","grid_cols":22,"grid_rows":5,"cell_width":720,"cell_height":404,"css_class_name":"set-1 white-background","published":true,"id":"5e965f716d6d6d8d094c0000","poster":"","cells":[{"title":"Overview Title Cell","description":".png image","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-background-color":"#61615C","css-background-size":"contain","class":"hide-info"},"id":"745701906d30343b53630000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Overview.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Overview.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Overview.png"}},"x":0,"y":0,"width":4,"height":5},{"title":"Overview Body Text 1","description":"Both Thomas Hauert and Bebe Miller are currently choreographing improvisation for performance and are engaging directly with the nature of human consciousness. When we watch them and their dancers, we are watching them at work. We are witness to the concentration and forms of attention that they bring to the moment and to how they work with their habits, tendencies, impulses, and memories in action.","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\">Both Thomas Hauert and Bebe Miller are currently choreographing improvisation for performance and are engaging directly with the nature of human consciousness. When we watch them and their dancers, we are watching them at work. We are witness to the concentration and forms of attention that they bring to the moment and to how they work with their habits, tendencies, impulses, and memories in action.</div>","css-background-color":"rgba(0,0,0,0.15)","css-color":"rgba(0,0,0,0.8)","css-font-size":"150%","css-overflow":"auto","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-padding-right":"3.5em"},"id":"9afc06906d30343b596e0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":4,"y":1,"width":2,"height":3},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH1","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-left-width":"0px","css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"864511906d30343b5c4c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/TH4.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/TH4.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/TH4.jpg"}},"x":6,"y":2,"width":1,"height":3},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH6","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"803712906d30343b53670000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Title-TH6.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Title-TH6.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Title-TH6.jpg"}},"x":7,"y":0,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH7","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"435412906d30343b597a0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Title-TH7-NEW.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Title-TH7-NEW.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Title-TH7-NEW.jpg"}},"x":8,"y":4,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH5","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"c66d12906d30343b597b0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Title-TH5-New.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Title-TH5-New.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Title-TH5-New.jpg"}},"x":9,"y":2,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Overview Call Out Text 1","description":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\">\r\n“Performing improvisation and the methods we have devised for rehearsing improvisation all arise from my desire to maximize the creative possibilities of the body in motion and to go beyond the habits inscribed in it.” \r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\">\r\n----- Thomas Hauert\r\n</div>\r\n</div>","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\"> “Performing improvisation and the methods we have devised for rehearsing improvisation all arise from my desire to maximize the creative possibilities of the body in motion and to go beyond the habits inscribed in it.”  <br> <div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\"> ----- Thomas Hauert </div> </div>","css-background-color":"#7E794B","css-color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.8)","css-font-size":"150%","css-overflow":"auto","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px"},"id":"284e17906d30343b56840000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":7,"y":2,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Overview Call Out Text 2","description":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\">\r\n“We are generating movement strategies that unfold in ways that are not as feasible in step-by-step choreography, for us. We specify the intentional body-mindset and allow the movement articulation — the dancing — to respond to the frame or strategy.” \r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\">\r\n----- Bebe Miller\r\n</div>\r\n</div>","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\"> “We are generating movement strategies that unfold in ways that are not as feasible in step-by-step choreography, for us. We specify the intentional body-mindset and allow the movement articulation — the dancing — to respond to the frame or strategy.”  <br> <div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\"> ----- Bebe Miller </div> </div>","css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","css-color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.8)","css-background-color":"#3E5FAB","css-overflow":"auto","css-font-size":"150%"},"id":"b0081b906d30343b597c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":10,"y":1,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Overview Image Title-BMC5","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"baef1e906d30343b536c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Title-BMC5.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Title-BMC5.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Title-BMC5.jpg"}},"x":12,"y":4,"width":3,"height":1},{"title":"Overview Call Out Text 3","description":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\">\r\n“My way of creating movement relies on the richness of human consciousness. In our dancing we explore the interaction between attention, focus, reflexes, conscious command, and sensory feedback.” \r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\">\r\n----- Thomas Hauert\r\n</div>\r\n</div>","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<div style=\"top:25%;position:relative\"> “My way of creating movement relies on the richness of human consciousness. In our dancing we explore the interaction between attention, focus, reflexes, conscious command, and sensory feedback.”  <br> <div style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,0.35)\"> ----- Thomas Hauert </div> </div>","css-overflow":"auto","css-font-size":"150%","css-color":"rgba(255,255,255,0.8)","css-background-color":"#3E6075","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white"},"id":"bb6a1f906d30343b597d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":14,"y":2,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH4","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"},"id":"40fa1f906d30343b56860000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/full/Title-TH4.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/small/Title-TH4.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/two/Cell/poster_image/medium/Title-TH4.jpg"}},"x":16,"y":0,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Overview Image Title-TH2","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"css-border-bottom-width":"3px","css-border-left-width":"3px","css-border-style":"solid","css-border-color":"white","class":"hide-info","css-background-size":"cover"